C03: a spoken opener before an order is request envelope (APPS1535)

«Y quema, abre Saint Rose.» reached no reader because of the transcription's opener «Y quema,»; without it, «abre Saint Rose» already receives the not-available answer for a name in no catalog. `_strip_request_envelope` now strips a conjunction, one word and a comma («Y quema,», «Y bueno,», «Y dale,») when an order head follows, as it already stripped the «sí,» of agreement; «y que…», «y si…» and «y no…» are left alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


